.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-storage-orphans - Diff claimed-vs-actual storage volumes for orphans


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge storage orphans <target-id> [storage-name] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Diff claimed-vs-actual storage volumes for orphans.

.PP
orphans is an advisory read. It diffs this node's storage content against the token VM list, so a vm-<vmid>-* volume whose VM is missing from that list — an in-flight or aborted create/clone, a permission-short token list, or a leftover — is reported as an orphan. Its output is not a list of volumes safe to delete.

.PP
storage free-orphans does not consume this list. It names a single VMID and re-derives what is unclaimed at free time from a root-sourced VM list under a quorum gate — stricter than this report — so a volume mis-listed for any other VMID is never freed. The allocate-before-registered and post-quorate residual for the freed VMID itself is a known deferred gap (pveforge-cluster-free-stale-shortlist-completeness), not closed by a lock. Do not feed this list to an external deleter without re-checking.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for orphans

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="kv"
	output format: "kv" or "json"

.PP
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-storage(1)\fP
